## Notes on Data Extraction & Gaps

- **Retail health GWP** and **Retail health market share**: Not separately disclosed as standalone line items in the statutory NL-return set; the Premium Schedule (NL-4) breaks premium down by Health/PA/Travel and Individual/Group categories, but does not isolate a single "Retail Health GWP" figure. Left blank per instructions rather than estimating.
- **PAT (IFRS basis)** and **Claims ratio (IFRS basis)**: Care Health Insurance's statutory filings are prepared under IGAAP only; no IFRS-basis figures are published in the IRDAI disclosure set, so these rows are blank.
- **Investment yield**: The Investment Schedule (Form 3A-equivalent) shows category-wise gross/net yields, but the OCR-derived Grand Total row could not be reconciled with sufficient confidence between quarterly and YTD income/investment figures. Per the strict "leave blank if not clearly verifiable" rule, this has been omitted rather than reporting an approximate/derived figure.
- **PAT reconciliation check**: The FY25 PAT of ₹155.18 crore was cross-verified by tracing the Reserves & Surplus schedule — opening P&L balance of ₹468.91 crore (carried from FY24) plus FY25 addition of ₹155.18 crore equals the closing balance of ₹624.09 crore, confirming consistency with the P&L Account.
- **NEP cross-check**: Net Earned Premium of ₹6,347.22 crore was derived from NWP (₹6,732.71 crore) + Opening UPR (₹2,893.70 crore) − Closing UPR (₹3,279.19 crore), and matches the figure independently reported in the NL-1 Revenue Account.
- All figures are for the **full year ended 31 March 2025** (cumulative YTD through Q4 FY24-25), sourced from the single Q4 FY24-25 Public Disclosure PDF, which is the statutory document carrying year-to-date figures inclusive of all four quarters.</ans>
